baseUrl= http://localhost:4000

HEALTH CHECK: GET {{baseUrl}}/health  

1) AUTH_REGISTER


### Register Citizen (default role = CITIZEN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Citizen One",
  "email": "citizen1@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Register Collector (will still register as CITIZEN, then you promote in DB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Collector One",
  "email": "collector1@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}


2) AUTH - LOGIN

### Login Citizen (copy token into @citizenToken below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "citizen1@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login Admin (only works AFTER you set role=ADMIN in DB for that user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login Collector (only works AFTER you set role=COLLECTOR in DB for that user)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "collector1@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}


 3) TOKENS (PASTE YOUR JWTs HERE)

@citizenToken =  token
@adminToken   = token
@collectorToken =  token


 4) USERS


### Who am I? (Citizen)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}

### Who am I? (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Who am I? (Collector)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{collectorToken}}


5) PICKUPS - CITIZEN


### Create Pickup (Citizen)
POST {{baseUrl}}/pickups
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}

{
  "address": "Nairobi CBD, Moi Avenue",
  "waste_type": "Plastic",
  "estimated_kg": 2.5
}

### Create Pickup (Citizen) - another sample
POST {{baseUrl}}/pickups
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}

{
  "address": "Westlands",
  "waste_type": "Glass",
  "estimated_kg": 3
}

### List My Pickups (Citizen)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pickups/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}


6) PICKUPS - ADMIN / COLLECTOR


### Available Pickups (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pickups/available
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Available Pickups (Collector)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pickups/available
Authorization: Bearer {{collectorToken}}

### Available Pickups (Citizen) - should be 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/pickups/available
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}


7) PICKUPS - ASSIGNMENT


### Assign Pickup (Admin) - replace :id
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pickups/3/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Assign Pickup (Collector) - sets collector_id to this collector
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pickups/3/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{collectorToken}}

### Assign Pickup (Citizen) - should be 403 Forbidden
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pickups/3/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}


8) PICKUPS - STATUS TRANSITIONS (COLLECTOR ONLY)

### NOTE:
### - /collect requires status ASSIGNED
### - /deliver requires status COLLECTED
### - ownership enforced: collector_id must match the token user id

### Mark COLLECTED (Collector)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pickups/3/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{collectorToken}}

### Mark DELIVERED (Collector)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pickups/3/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{collectorToken}}

### Negative: Deliver before Collect (should be 400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pickups/3/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{collectorToken}}

### Negative: Collector tries to change pickup they don't own (should be 403)
### (Only meaningful if pickup 3 is assigned to a different collector_id)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pickups/3/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{collectorToken}}


9) OPTIONAL: ADMIN DASHBOARD (IF YOU ADDED IT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Negative: Citizen to admin dashboard (should be 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}
